{
  "name": "vrp-stayintent-pages-v0.1",
  "protocol_version": "0.1",
  "description": "Pages (spec/stayintent-discovery-v0.1.md §4.4) and the endpoint a node names in its discovery document (§10). chains[].pages are the pages of one chain in reading order; expected.reason is null for a chain a client accepts, else the name of the first rule it breaks (§4.4; not_response, ranking_signal, monetary_value, trust_summary_not_fact, cursor_invalid, match_count_invalid, cursor_missing, empty_page_with_cursor, chain_open, duplicate_node, not_ascending, match_flag_wrong, match_count_mismatch). endpoints[].value are values of endpoints.stayintent (an array of one to ten https URLs, a set); reasons not_array, empty, too_many_entries, not_string, url_invalid, url_not_https, url_userinfo, duplicate_entry. Whether an address is globally reachable (§10) is a runtime check, not a vector. Example domains only; no implementation or real node is named.",
